<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Greina crossing via Terrihütte — Puzzatsch–Pass Diesrut–Terrihütte–Runcahez</name><desc>Cross Pass Diesrut from Puzzatsch, take Punt la Greina to Terrihütte, then descend via Crest la Greina and Alp da Tenigia to the Runcahez reservoir. Usually a two-day summer crossing with an overnight hut stay; chains protect short rocky descent sections. Confirm the actual Runcahez pickup when reserving the bus. If the Acla Mulin diversion is active, use the signed suspension bridge and allow about 40 extra minutes beyond this attached route. Recheck hut, snow and weather before departure.

